<font style=3D"font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif;" size=3D"2">Hi
Marcel,<br /><br />thank you for your answer. I need Skype because all
my friends use Skype. It's right that SIP is the VOIP Standard, but my
friends use Skype and under Windows it works perfectly. I want to kick
windows from my hdd in near future. The OSS-Version of Skype works
perfectly with my internal sound card not the alsa-version.
Unfortunately i dont' know how to use the oss- version with bluez. The
.asoundrc can emulate a dsp device but i do not understand the use of
this file. The alsa wiki describes with examples the use of .asoundrc
but i cannot adopt these examples to bluez. It's too strange for me.
Mplayer runs fine with bluez and my headset but 8 khz sound is not
really hifi :-) I have read in some linux lists that the old btso kernel
driver works fine with skype but i don't want to use an obsolete driver.
Therefore it should somehow be possible to use it with the current
version of bluez. I have tested kphone which is a sip-phone. Also kphone
doesn' t work with my headset. I spent many hours to make a call with my
headset until my wife asked me if i was totally crazy. She started
windows and in 5 minutes she could speak to friends with this headset
and skype. It was a disgrace :-(<br /><br /><br />Regards<br />Frank<br
/><br />
